{
  "an3.156:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.156–162 ",
  "an3.156:0.2": "The Chapter on Practices ",
  "an3.156:0.3": "Untitled Discourses on Three Practices ",
  "an3.156:1.1": "“Mendicants, there are three practices. ",
  "an3.156:1.2": "What three? ",
  "an3.156:1.3": "The addicted practice, the scorching practice, and the middle practice. ",
  "an3.156:1.4": "And what’s the addicted practice? ",
  "an3.156:1.5": "It’s when someone has this doctrine and view: ",
  "an3.156:1.6": "‘There’s nothing wrong with sensual pleasures’; ",
  "an3.156:1.7": "so they throw themselves into sensual pleasures. ",
  "an3.156:1.8": "This is called the addicted practice. ",
  "an3.156:2.1": "And what’s the scorching practice? ",
  "an3.156:2.2": "It’s when someone goes naked, ignoring conventions. They lick their hands, and don’t come or wait when called. They don’t consent to food brought to them, or food prepared on their behalf, or an invitation for a meal. ",
  "an3.156:2.3": "They don’t receive anything from a pot or bowl; or from someone who keeps sheep, or who has a weapon or a shovel in their home; or where a couple is eating; or where there is a woman who is pregnant, breastfeeding, or who lives with a man; or where there’s a hound waiting or flies buzzing. They accept no fish or meat or beer or wine, and drink no fermented gruel. ",
  "an3.156:2.4": "They go to just one house for alms, taking just one mouthful, or two houses and two mouthfuls, up to seven houses and seven mouthfuls. ",
  "an3